# 3-arg case: dot-access expression in pattern position hits the exact-value fallback.
# CoreExpr::DotAccess is not a literal or constructor, so eval_structural_pattern_inner
# evaluates n.x in the outer env (pin semantics) and compares to scrutinee.
# n.x = 5, scrutinee = 5 → match. Demonstrates the generic exact-value fallback path.
[n: [x: 5  y: 3]]
[match 5
  [case [let] n.x "matched-x"]
  [case [let] _ "other"]]
=== out
String("matched-x")
